 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? Most people learn it through studying or traveling in a German speaking country. Work is often the next biggest source. Yes, lots of common nouns end in e in German, just like in English. It is, but it works. Another trick is to memorise a list of about fifty common words, you'll reach lots of 'er's. Memorise a list of common words, repeat nouns more than other ends of words, and learn proper pronunciation. Gender makes much more sense then. Green for gas, yellow for oil, and red for water. It actually helps once you know.",
